### \`tls.m.image\` — Image

Image with cover/contain fit, focal point, and optional caption. _(family: media; keywords: image, photo, picture, media, visual)_

**When:** Use to display a photograph, screenshot, or illustration with optional caption.
**Avoid:** Do not use for charts — use tls.d.bar. Do not use for placeholder backgrounds — use tls.l.field.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`src\` | yes | image | Asset id or URL of the image to display. |
| \`alt\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | 1–10 words describing what the image shows. |
| \`fit\` | no | enum: cover \\\\| contain | How the image fills its box: cover (crop to fill) or contain (letterbox). |
| \`focal\` | no | object (fx, fy) | Focus area when fit is \\"cover\\". Default is center [0.5, 0.5]. |
| \`caption\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | Optional caption displayed below the image. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_image\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.m.image\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"src\\": \\"asset-hero-photo\\",
    \\"alt\\": \\"Team meeting in conference room\\",
    \\"fit\\": \\"cover\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"Team offsite, Q3 2026\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.body\` — Body

Paragraph body text with RichText, autofit, and multi-column. _(family: text; keywords: body, paragraph, text, prose, copy, description)_

**When:** Use for 1–3 sentences of body copy, descriptions, or prose.
**Avoid:** Do not use for bullet lists (use tls.t.bullets) or captions (use tls.t.caption).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A concise paragraph, 1–3 sentences. Use bold for key terms. |
| \`columns\` | no | number (min 1, max 4) | Number of text columns. 1 = single paragraph. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`autoFit\` | no | boolean | Shrink font when content overflows the box. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_body\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.body\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Design systems scale because every \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"decision\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\" is made once.\\"
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"columns\\": 1,
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.bullets\` — Bullet list

Bullet list with dot/dash/chevron/number markers and indent levels. _(family: text; keywords: bullets, list, items, points, markers, unordered)_

**When:** Use for 2–8 short items that the audience should scan, not read.
**Avoid:** Do not use for sentences of prose — use tls.t.body. More than 8 items means two slides.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of text (1–40 items) | 2–8 items, each 2–8 words. Start each with a verb or noun, not a full sentence. |
| \`marker\` | no | enum: dot \\\\| dash \\\\| chevron \\\\| number \\\\| icon | Bullet style. |
| \`indentLevels\` | no | boolean | Enable per-item indent levels for nested lists. |
| \`spacing\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg | Vertical spacing between items. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_bullets\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.bullets\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Revenue up 42% YoY\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Enterprise APAC drove growth\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Churn fell to 3.1%\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"marker\\": \\"dot\\",
    \\"spacing\\": \\"sm\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.caption\` — Caption

Small caption text for images, charts, and media. _(family: text; keywords: caption, subtitle, description, label, small-text, source)_

**When:** Use to label a chart, image, or data source — 5–15 words maximum.
**Avoid:** Do not use for body text or slide titles.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | A brief description, 5–15 words. State what the reader should notice. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`position\` | no | enum: below \\\\| above \\\\| overlay | Where the caption sits relative to its referenced content. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_cap\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.caption\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"Source: internal Q3 financials\\",
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.hero-number\` — Hero Number

Large KPI number with optional unit and caption. _(family: text; keywords: kpi, number, stat, metric, hero, display, count)_

**When:** Use for one standout metric ($4.2M, 67%) that anchors a KPI slide.
**Avoid:** Do not use for multiple metrics in a row — use a grid of hero-numbers instead.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | no | text | The headline number. Include formatting, e.g. \\"$4.2M\\", \\"67%\\", \\"1,234\\". |
| \`unit\` | no | text | Unit label, 1–4 words. e.g. \\"Annual Revenue\\", \\"Completion Rate\\". |
| \`caption\` | no | text | Short context, 1 line max. e.g. \\"FY2024 total\\", \\"vs. last quarter\\". |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number format hint for the renderer. |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: default \\\\| accent \\\\| muted | Colour emphasis for the headline number. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.hero-number\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": \\"$4.2M\\",
    \\"unit\\": \\"Annual Revenue\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"FY2024 total\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"currency\\",
    \\"emphasis\\": \\"accent\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.kicker\` — Kicker

Small label above the title with case and tracking options. _(family: text; keywords: kicker, eyebrow, label, category, tag, section)_

**When:** Use as a small category or section label above the title.
**Avoid:** Do not use for the slide title itself — use tls.t.title.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | text (max 60 chars) | A short label: section name, category, or status. UPPERCASE by default. 1–4 words. |
| \`case\` | no | enum: uppercase \\\\| lowercase \\\\| capitalize \\\\| none | Text transformation. Defaults to uppercase. |
| \`tracking\` | no | enum: wide \\\\| normal \\\\| narrow | Letter spacing for the kicker text. |
| \`marker\` | no | boolean | Show a small accent dot before the text. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kicker\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.kicker\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"OVERVIEW\\",
    \\"case\\": \\"uppercase\\",
    \\"tracking\\": \\"wide\\",
    \\"marker\\": false
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.quote\` — Quote

Pull quote with decorative quotation glyph, attribution, and role. _(family: text; keywords: quote, blockquote, pull-quote, attribution, testimonial)_

**When:** Use to feature a direct quote with attribution from a named person.
**Avoid:** Do not use for anonymous insights — use tls.t.takeaway instead.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | no | richText | The quoted text. Can be 1–3 sentences. |
| \`attribution\` | no | text | Name of the person being quoted. |
| \`role\` | no | text | Title or role of the attributed person. |
| \`markStyle\` | no | enum: glyph \\\\| rule \\\\| none | How the quotation mark is rendered. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_quote\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.quote\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"The only way to do great work is to love what you do.\\",
    \\"attribution\\": \\"Steve Jobs\\",
    \\"role\\": \\"Co-founder, Apple\\",
    \\"markStyle\\": \\"glyph\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.subtitle\` — Subtitle

Secondary heading below the title with RichText support. _(family: text; keywords: subtitle, subheading, secondary)_

**When:** Use to add context, date, or audience below the title.
**Avoid:** Do not use for long paragraphs — use tls.t.body instead.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A brief supporting sentence or phrase. 3–12 words. Never repeat the title. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_sub\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.subtitle\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Q3 FY2026 · prepared for the \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"board\\",
          \\"italic\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.takeaway\` — Takeaway

Highlighted insight text with accent bar and optional label. _(family: text; keywords: takeaway, insight, callout, highlight, key-point)_

**When:** Use to call out a key insight, conclusion, or \\"so what\\" from data.
**Avoid:** Do not use for quotes from named people — use tls.t.quote instead.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | no | richText | The insight or takeaway. 1–2 sentences, direct and clear. |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| positive \\\\| warning \\\\| muted | Visual tone that controls the accent bar and surface tint. |
| \`icon\` | no | icon | Optional icon shown beside the label. |
| \`label\` | no | text | Short label, 1–3 words. e.g. \\"Key Insight\\", \\"Remember\\". |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_take\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.takeaway\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"Compute spend grew 2.4x while revenue grew 1.2x.\\",
    \\"tone\\": \\"accent\\",
    \\"label\\": \\"Key Insight\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.title\` — Title

Slide title with inline styling, autofit, and truncation. _(family: text; keywords: title, heading, hero, headline, slide)_

**When:** Use as the primary heading on every content slide — the single most important text.
**Avoid:** Do not use for section dividers (use tls.c.hero instead) or subtitles.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A concise slide title. Bold one key word for emphasis. Never a full sentence. |
| \`size\` | no | enum: display \\\\| title \\\\| heading \\\\| subheading | Type scale step for the title. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`rule\` | no | boolean | Show a short accent rule below the title. |
| \`maxLines\` | no | number (min 1, max 10) | Maximum number of lines before truncation. Truncation adds a visible marker. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_title\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.title\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Revenue \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"grew 42%\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"size\\": \\"title\\",
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Worked example — a valid slide

Zero coordinates, zero colour values, zero font sizes. Region names come from the layout (\`two-column\` → \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\`); block types and slots come from the tables above.

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"sl_03\\",
  \\"layout\\": \\"two-column\\",
  \\"role\\": \\"content\\",
  \\"rhythm\\": \\"dense\\",
  \\"regions\\": {
    \\"title\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b1\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.title\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": {
            \\"runs\\": [
              {
                \\"text\\": \\"Margin fell on \\"
              },
              {
                \\"text\\": \\"infrastructure\\",
                \\"bold\\": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    \\"left\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b2\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.bar\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"categories\\": [
            \\"Q1\\",
            \\"Q2\\",
            \\"Q3\\"
          ],
          \\"series\\": [
            64,
            64,
            61
          ],
          \\"highlightIndex\\": 2
        },
        \\"motion\\": {
          \\"preset\\": \\"bars-grow\\",
          \\"order\\": 2,
          \\"trigger\\": \\"onClick\\"
        }
      }
    ],
    \\"right\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b3\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.takeaway\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": \\"Compute spend grew 2.4× while revenue grew 1.2×.\\"
        },
        \\"motion\\": {
          \\"preset\\": \\"fade-up\\",
          \\"order\\": 3
        }
      },
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b4\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.caption\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": \\"Source: internal Q3 financials\\"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  \\"notes\\": \\"Land on the 61 — this is the hinge slide.\\"
}
\`\`\`
"
`;

